<title>USA: Coca-Cola Co Q4 shr $0.31 vs $0.26.</title>
<headline>Coca-Cola Co Q4 shr $0.31 vs $0.26.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In Millions, except per share data)</p>
<p>						   Fourth Quarter</p>
<p>					     1996	  1995  % Change</p>
<p> Net operating revenues		$4,443     $4,333	3 %</p>
<p> Net income				   762	  648	 18</p>
<p> Net income per share		    0.31	0.26*	 19</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding	   2,485     2,507*	(1)</p>
<p>*  Net income per share and average shares outstanding have been adjusted to reflect a two-for-one stock split, effective May 1, 1996.</p>
<p>				  Twelve Months Ended December 31</p>
<p>						1996	 1995  % Change</p>
<p> Net operating revenues	     $18,546    $18,018	 3%</p>
<p> Net income				 3,492	2,986	 17</p>
<p> Net income per share		    1.40	1.18*	 19</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding	   2,494     2,525*	(1)</p>
<p>* Net income per share and average shares outstanding have been adjusted to reflect a two-for-one stock split, effective May 1, 1996.</p>
<p>The company was expected to earn $0.31 per share for the fourth quarter, based on the average estimate by analysts surveyed by First Call. For the year, the estimate was $1.40 per share.</p>
</text>
